---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base
  title="About Felipe Cabral"
  description="Felipe Cabral. Fifteen years across startups, engineering leadership and civic tech, from Porto Alegre to Stockholm."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="display">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="column prose about">
      <p class="lede">I'm Felipe Cabral. I live in Stockholm and I work on data and AI systems.</p>
      <p>
        I started in Porto Alegre in 2011, co-founding Engage, a studio that built early-stage
        products and helped ignite a lot of what became the Brazilian startup scene. That work
        turned into data science consulting, and then into Serenata de Amor and a run of civic tech
        projects across Brazil, Italy and Canada: turning unreadable government datasets into files
        a journalist could open, and rebuilding Montreal's open data portal with Datopian.
      </p>
      <p>
        I moved to Sweden and moved through engineering leadership. Technical director at Essen,
        CTO at Ares Habitats, then consulting through Accelerated Growth AB at IKEA and now Tetra
        Pak.
      </p>
      <p>
        The through-line is that I keep ending up in the same place: somewhere there's data nobody
        can act on, and someone has to build the thing that makes it usable.
      </p>
      <p>
        I studied business administration at PUCRS, not engineering, which meant learning to build
        by building. I've practised Aikido for over twenty years. That's had more influence on how I
        work than any methodology I've read, mostly around not forcing things that aren't ready to
        move.
      </p>
    </div>

    <dl class="contact column">
      <div class="field"><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></dd></div>
      <div class="field"><dt>Elsewhere</dt><dd><a href={site.linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .contact {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
  }

  @media (min-width: 560px) {
    .contact {
      grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .contact dd {
    font: var(--title);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>
